From bf619ecb49c45820c18815ed122968558e65bf06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Kaminski MVP <Kevin.Kaminski@bighatgroup.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 13:58:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(external-hooks): let PreCompact hooks return a validated
 prune decision

The PreCompact payload now carries the agent history in a hook-safe
projection (agent_id, max_context_tokens, instruction, and messages with
per-entry text capped at 200 000 characters) so an external program can
score the conversation. On exit 0 a hook may print
hookSpecificOutput.compactionDecision "prune" with a prune object listing
tool call ids to drop and tool results to truncate; the decision is
validated against the live history (unknown ids, open tool exchanges,
duplicate ids, and bad headChars are rejected and logged) and the first
valid decision among parallel hooks is carried on the compaction task for
the compaction service to apply. Existing hooks keep working: new fields
are additive, malformed or absent output compacts as before, and exit code
2 stays non-blocking. Docs (en and zh) describe the payload, the decision
shape, and the validation rules.
